This is a sample USERIN file for running the EPS3 system.
The file is separated into packets.  The packet identifier
is a keyword surrounded by a forward slash (/) character.  The
packet terminator is /END/.  The packet identifies are
not case sensitive. A packet can be disabled by
putting any non-blank character (for example a ; ) in the first
column of the packet identifier.  Packets can appear in any
order and any notes can be placed between packet identifiers.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the packet that defines the species list that will
be generated in the inventory.  The species name and the
molecular weight of the species are defined here, as well as
the criteria pollutant associated with the species.  Only
those species in the list will be included in the inventory.

The fields are:

 1-20 label (ignored)
21-30 species name
31-40 name of associated criteria pollutant
41-50 molecular weight

/SPECIES LIST/
                   :NO         NOX         46.0
                   :NO2        NOX         46.0
                   :OLE        VOC         32.0
                   :PAR        VOC         16.0
                   :TOL        VOC        112.0
                   :XYL        VOC        128.0
                   :FORM       VOC         16.0
                   :ALD2       VOC         32.0
                   :ETH        VOC         32.0
                   :MEOH       VOC         16.0
                   :ETOH       VOC         32.0
                   :ISOP       VOC         80.0
                   :CO         CO          28.0
/END/

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the packet that defines the data and time of the inventory.
The date should be calendar date of the form yymmdd
The beginning and ending time are 2 digit hours.

The fields are:
Line 1: 1-20 label (ignored)
Line 1: 21-80 inventory note (arbitrary string)
Line 2: 1-20 label (ignored)
Line 2: 21-30 inventory date - yymmdd
Line 2: 1-20 label (ignored)
Line 2: 21-30 beginning time (0 = first hour of the day)
Line 3: 1-20 label (ignored)
Line 3: 21-30 ending time (24 = last hour of the day)

/DATE/
Inventory Note     :CAMx Modeling of Tx regional, 9/13/99
Inventory Date     :990913
Beginning Time     : 0
Ending Time        : 24
/END/

----------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the packet that defines the modeling domain.
The units should be in km for UTM or Polar Stereographic 
and Decimal degrees for Geodesic coordinates. 

The fields are:
Line 1:  1-20  label (ignored)
Line 1:  21-30 Origin in X direction
Line 1:  31-40 Origin in Y direction
Line 2:  1-20  label (ignored)
Line 2:  21-30 UTM zone (put 0 for non-UTM coordinates)
Line 3:  1-20  label (ignored)
Line 3:  21-30 Cell Width in X direction
Line 3:  31-40 Cell Width in Y direction
Line 4:  1-20  label (ignored)
Line 4:  21-30 Number of cells in X direction
Line 4:  31-40 Number of cells in Y direction

/REGION/
Domain Origin      :-108.00   -1584.00
UTM Zone           :0
Cell Width         :12.0      12.0
Number of Cells    :135       138
Projection Type    : LAMBERT
Pole Longitude     :     -97.0
Pole Latitude      :      40.0
1st True Latitude  :      33.0
2nd Tru Latitude   :      45.0
/END/

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the packet that defines the default split factors.  If a 
constant value is used to split a species from its parent criteria
pollutant then it should be placed here.  The splits file should
be used for species that vary by source category.  If all species
are split using constants then then it is not necessary to supply
a splits file of lookup table file.  All of the data can be defined
is this packet.  The CHMSPL program will only know about species
found either here or in the splits file.

The fields are:
1-20   label (ignored)
21-30  species to create
31-40  the parent criteria pollutant from which to split it
41-50  split factor (converts from grams of criteria to moles of species)

/DEFAULT SPLITS/
Nitrous Oxides     : NO       NOX       90
Nitrous Oxides     : NO2      NOX       10
Carbon Monoxide    : CO       CO        100
/END/
Sulfur Dioxide     : SO2      SOX       97
Fine PM            : PFIN    PM25       100 
Coarse PM          : PCRS    PM10       100 
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the packet that is used to define the criteria pollutants
that will be in the inventory files read by PREAM/PREPNT.  The
information from this packet will be carried in the EMBR file so
no other module needs to read it.  The fields are:

 1-20  label (ignored)
21-30  name of criteria pollutant
31-40  SAROAD code of this pollutant.

The names can be arbitrary but the SAROAD codes must match the
codes in the input inventory files.  Only these pollutants will
be included in the output inventory.

/CRITERIA POLLUTANT/
Nitrous Oxides     : NOx       42603
Carbon Dioxide     : CO        42101
HydroCarbons       : VOC       43104
/END/
Sulfur             : SOX       42401
Particulates > 10  : PM10      11101
Particulates < 10  : PM25      81102
/END/
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the packet that tells the modules what tables to produce for
the criteria pollutants.  If the name of a module appears on the a
line, then that module will produce the indicated table.  If the 
packet is missing then only the default tables (brief summaries of
processes emissions) will be produced.  By putting a comma next
to the module name you can have the module produce a separate CSV
file containing the table, in addition to the formatted table written
to the message file.

The module names can appear in any order on a line, in mixed case.  
However, the order of the lines is important.  The order must be:

By County
By Source Category
By County and Source Category
By Hour
Source Category and Hour
County and Facility
County, Facility and Stack
County, Facility, Stack and Point

The names of the modules should be:

PREAM
PREPNT
CHMSPL
CNTLEM
TMPRL
GRDEM
PSTPNT

/CRITERIA TABLES/
County             : PrePNT Pream TMPRL CNTLEM
Source Category    : Prepnt pream GRDEM
County and Src Cat : Grdem,
Hour               : Tmprl,
Src Cat and Hour   : Lbase
County and Facility: prepnt
Cty, Fac and Stk   : prepnt
Cty, Fac, Stk, Pnt : prepnt
/END/

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the packet that tells the modules what tables to produce for
the model species.  If the name of a module appears on the a
line, then that module will produce the indicated table.  If the
packet is missing then only the default tables (brief summaries of
processes emissions) will be produced.  By putting a comma next
to the module name you can have the module produce a separate CSV
file containing the table, in addition to the formatted table written
to the message file.

The module names can appear in any order on a line, in mixed case.  
However, the order of the lines is important.  The order must be:


By County
By Source Category
By County and Source Category
By Hour
Source Category and Hour
County and Facility
County, Facility and Stack
County, Facility, Stack and Point

The names of the modules should be:

PREAM
PREPNT
CHMSPL
CNTLEM
TMPRL
GRDEM
PSTPNT

;  /SPECIES TABLES/
County             : 
Source Category    : 
County and Src Cat : 
Hour               : 
Src Cat and Hour   :
County and Facility: 
Cty, Fac and Stk   : 
Cty, Fac, Stk, Pnt :
/END/

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the parameters specific to the TMPRL module.

The fields are:

Line 1:  1-20  Label (ignored)
Line 1: 21-25  Day of the week for this inventory
(MON, TUE, WED, THU, FRI, SAT, SUN)
Line 2:  1-20  Label (ignored)
Line 2: 21-25  Photochemical modeling time zone (zone under which the
model will be run)
(PST, MST, CST, EST, PDT, MDT, CDT, EDT) 

/TMPRL/
Day of Week        : MON
Time Zone          : CST
/END/

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the parameters specific to the PREPNT module.
The first parameter determines whether the coordinates of the point
source locations should be converted during the PREPNT processing.
The only conversion supported is geodesic to UTM. The second parameter
indicates whether records with missing stack parameters should be
processed.  If this is set to YES, the other parameters define the default 
stack parameters that will be used in place of the missing values
on the input record.  The plume height cutoff determines the height
at which a source is flagged as an elevated source.  This is used as
an initial screening to minimize the number of elevated sources fed
to the photochemical model.

The fields are:
Line 1:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 1: 21-25  Flag to determine if input stack coordinates should be converted
Line 2:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 2: 21-25  Flag to determine if records with missing stacks will be processed
Line 3:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 3: 21-30  Plume height cutoff (meters) 
Line 4:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 4: 21-30  Default stack height (meters)
Line 5:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 5: 21-30  Default stack diameter (meters)
Line 6:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 6: 21-30  Default stack gas exit temperature (degrees K)
Line 7:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 7: 21-30  Default stack gas exit velocity (meters/second)


/PREPNT/
Convert Coordinates: NO
Process Missing stk: YES
Plume ht Cutoff (M): 50.0
Default stk ht (M) : 3.0
Default diam (M)   : 0.2
Default temp (K)   : 294.
Default veloc (M/S): 0.5
/END/


----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the parameters specific to the LBASE module.
This flag determines if the input link-based emissions files contains
grams or tons.

The fields are:

 1-20  Label (ignored)
21-25  Units for link-based emissions 
       (GRAMS or TONS)

/LBASE/
Units of Input Emis:Grams
/END/



----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the parameters specific to the CHMSPL module.
Each is a flag.  The first flag determines if CHMSPL should process
the inventory even if the species list is not an exact match with the
species list in the split factors file. Typically, the split factors
file contains additional species that are considered non-reactive.
The second flag tells CHMSPL to print an emissions summary table
by speciation profile code. The last flag will allow CHMSPL to process
source categories that have no match in the speciation lookup table.
If set to NO, any sources that have no match will be processed using
the "overall average" profile which is designated as profile code 0000.

The fields are:

Line 1:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 1: 21-25  Flag for processing mismatched species lists
Line 2:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 2: 21-25  Flag to print an emissions summary table by profile code
Line 3:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 3: 21-25  Flag to force all source categories to be included in the
               speciation lookup table

/CHMSPL/
Use Non-match Specs: YES
Print Profile Table: YES
Force Profile Match: YES
/END/

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the parameters specific to the GRDEM module.
The first flag determines if the output should be a CAMx model-ready 
emissions file or an EPS3 EMBR file.  If set to YES, the inventory
must at the proper stage of processing (speciated and temporally 
allocated). The second flag determines if the secondary and tertiary
surrogates should be used.

The fields are:

Line 1:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 1: 21-25  Flag for type of output file to create 
               (YES = CAMx model ready)
Line 2:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 2: 21-25  Flag to turn on secondary surrogates.

/GRDEM/
Output is CAMx     : YES
Use Secondary Surgs: NO
/END/

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the parameters specific to the CNTLEM module.
This flag determines if a tables of processed emissions should
be written for each county. This can be a lot of data written to
the message file, but is useful for analyzing a control strategy. 

The fields are:

Line 1:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 1: 21-25  Flag to determine if tables by county should be 
               written to the message file

/CNTLEM/
Print County Tables: YES
/END/

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the parameters specific to the CNTLEM module.
This flag determines if the headers of the emissions files being
merged should be checked for consistency, resulting in termination
of inconsistencies are found. If this is turned off, the headers
will still be checked but inconsistencies will only result in a
warning, which is written to the message file.

The fields are:

Line 1:  1-20  Label (not used)
Line 1: 21-25  Flag to determine if header inconsistencies result
               in errors or warnings
               (YES = inconsistency will terminate the program)

/MRGUAM/
Check Header flag  :NO
/END/
  
----------------------------------------------------------------
This packet contains the list of counties to be processed.  It
is accessed by almost all of the modules and utilities. You must
specify a 5-digit FIPS code and a time-zone identifier. Only 
time zones in the US are supported.  The time zone is used by 
the TMPRL module to shift to the time zone used in the 
photochemical modeling.

The fields are: 
1-20  label (ignored)
21-25 FIPS code of the county
27-30 time zone for the county 
(PST, MST, CST, EST, PDT, MDT, CDT, EDT) 

